Suite: Rate watch
  Rate watch shows the latest exchange rate for a pair of currencies, such as euros to dollars,
  and tells you when the rate reaches a level you chose.

Vocabulary:
  # The rate comes from an outside provider. The app can't control it, so its health is a state.
  State: the rate feed is live | delayed | unavailable
    Set: switch the test provider to {value}
    Shows: live: the rate has a green dot
    Shows: delayed: the rate has an amber dot and says when it was last updated
    Shows: unavailable: the rate is replaced by the message "Rates unavailable" and a Retry button
  State: the alert is off | waiting | triggered
    Shows: off: the Alert button reads "Set alert"
    Shows: waiting: the Alert button reads "Alert set"
    Shows: triggered: a banner says the rate reached your target
  Event: the user sets an alert
    Say: type a target rate and tap Set alert
  Event: the feed falls behind
    Say: make the test provider send rates late
  Event: the feed stops answering
    Say: switch the test provider off
  Event: the feed answers again
    Say: switch the test provider back on and tap Retry
  Event: the rate reaches the target
    Say: have the test provider send a rate at or past your target

  Term: Target rate
    The rate at which you want to be told. An alert watches one pair of currencies and has one target.
  Term: Rate provider
    The outside service that sends the exchange rates. Rate watch only shows what the provider sends.
    Reference: Provider API | https://example.com/docs/rates

Background:
  Given the rate feed is live
  And the alert is off
